g the `lsbit` 3-way branch\n   (`lsbit == 4` / `lsbit & 1` / else) and the two candidate-clamp tests.\n7. The final selection: C does `if (d1 < d0) uni = uni1; if (d2 < d0) uni = uni2;` — BOTH compared\n   against the ORIGINAL d0, and the second `if` can overwrite the first. Verify the Rust replicates\n   this exactly (it must NOT use a running best).\n8. Whether the C's unused variable `p3` affects anything.\n9. Any place the Rust could panic (overflow check in debug, shift overflow, division overflow) where\n   the C would not.\n10. The FFI signature: parameter order, types, return type, `#[no_mangle]`, `extern \"C\"`.\n\nReport ONLY concrete findings in this format:\n- A numbered list of any REAL behavioral differences you found (with the exact C line, the exact Rust\n  line, and a concrete input tuple (uni, step, pred, tgt, tgt2, lsbit) that would produce different\n  results). If you find none, say \"NO BEHAVIORAL DIFFERENCES FOUND\" explicitly.\n- Then a short list of anything you were UNSURE about and why.\n\nBe skeptical and precise. Do not claim equivalence without actually checking each item above."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":415,"cache_read_input_tokens":128494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":415,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a91fdee-45d7-4693-8d7e-88ac17e9e078","uuid":"d8a5c0ad-cc6d-4e90-8e31-9863c84821ae","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:23:53.444Z"}
