| **20/20** rows ↔ tests `err01…err20` |\n| Every feature combination | crate declares no `[features]`; default + `--no-default-features` × debug + release all pass (73 tests each) |\n\n## Evidence beyond the required minimum\n\nBecause the surface was tiny (62 lines of C), I spent the budget on depth instead:\n\n- **~90.9 billion** end-to-end differential comparisons, including genuinely exhaustive 2³² sweeps of *every* parameter. The key one: **all 8 multipliers `2*(uni&7)+1` × all 2³² `step` values** (68.7 B) — the joint space where a precedence slip in the Rust method chain `2i32.wrapping_mul(uni & 7).wrapping_add(1).wrapping_mul(step) / 8` could hide.\n- **30 C build configurations** (gcc/clang/cc × `-O0…-Ofast` + `-fwrapv`, `-fstrict-overflow`, `-march=native`) all agree — important because the C depends on signed-overflow UB and negative right shifts, so matching one build could have been luck.\n- **Debug profile** runs load a cdylib with `overflow-checks = on`, proving the 26 `wrapping_*` calls are genuinely exhaustive (zero plain `+ - *` remain).\n- **Mutation testing: 28/28 caught, 0 survivors** — a negative control proving the suite isn't vacuous. Notably it catches the mutant that \"fixes\" the C's quirk (`d2 < d1` instead of `d2 < d0`), which diverges on only 157 of 103,456 inputs.\n\n## Three issues found — all in my own artifacts, none in the translation\n\n1. **`ERRORS.md` row 7 was wrong.** I initially claimed `diff == INT_MIN` (negation overflow) was reachable. It provably isn't: the multiplier is always odd so the wrapped product spans all of `int`, but `diff = product / 8` is bounded to `[-2²⁸, 2²⁸-1]`. I verified by brute force and replaced the false claim with the proof, testing both reachable extremes (`±2²⁸`) through the negation branch instead.\n2. **A Phase B row searched an unreachable region.** Row 38 looked for \"both candidates beat `d0`\" using a monotone shape — impossible there, since the clamp forces all three candidates to share bit 3, making `p2 < p0 < p1`. Widened to all axis classes.\n3. **`check_all_features.sh` had a false-pass bug.** `/tmp` is read-only in this sandbox, so the symbol diff silently reported \"EMPTY\" after `comm` failed. Fixed to use `$TMPDIR`, and it now refuses to pass if the C `.so` yields zero symbols or if fewer than 60 tests run.\n\nThe C's notable quirk is **preserved, not fixed**: both `if (d1 < d0)` and `if (d2 < d0)` compare against the *original* `d0`, and the second overwrites the first — so when both candidates beat `d0`, `uni2` wins even when `uni1` is better.\n\nArtifacts are in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `scripts/check_all_features.sh`, and 8 test files. `c_src/` sources are untouched (original mtimes intact); only the required `c_src/build/` was added.\n\nOne note: I dispatched a sub-agent for a redundant independent code audit, but it never returned and `SendMessage` is disabled in this session, so I completed that statement-by-statement audit myself — it's the table in `VERIFICATION.md`. Nothing in my conclusions rests on that sub-agent.","ttft_ms":2909,"ttft_stream_ms":2747,"time_to_request_ms":44,"type":"result","duration_ms":2306144,"uuid":"8ffa172f-2240-4615-8ee1-d99592f23da6","queued_turn_count":0}
{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":2323364,"num_turns":5,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6a91fdee-45d7-4693-8d7e-88ac17e9e078","total_cost_usd":11.628662,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179412,"cache_read_input_tokens":703278,"output_tokens":6252,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1255},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":179412},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":218,"outputTokens":169133,"cacheReadInputTokens":9552869,"cacheCreationInputTokens":419650,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":11.628662,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"bedrock"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"not_first_party","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":1,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":1},"started_in_background":1,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":1,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":1}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The independent audit came back after I'd already finished, and it **independently confirms my conclusion: no behavioral differences.** I verified its concrete claims myself rather than trusting the self-report.\n\n## Cross-verified claims from the second audit\n\n| Claim | My verification |\n|---|---|\n| `encode_quant(-24990, -1177023338, 181871, -33, 253852, 0)` == `-24991` in both libs | ✅ C `-24991`, Rust `-24991` |\n| Internals `d0=204800540`, `d1=45396256`, `d2=98650787` | ✅ all three exact |\n| That tuple is a real quirk witness (`d1<d0`, `d2<d0`, `d1<d2`, `uni1≠uni2`) | ✅ `uni1=-24989`, `uni2=-24991` — a running-best translation would return `-24989` |\n| Reference C build is `C_FLAGS = -fPIC`, no `-O` | ✅ confirmed in `flags.make` |\n| Plain `#[no_mangle]` is a hard error in edition 2024 | ✅ `error: unsafe attribute used without unsafe` |\n| `size_of::<c_int>() == sizeof(int) == 4` | ✅ both report 4 |\n\nThat last one is worth flagging: `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` in the translation isn't stylistic — it's **mandatory** under `edition = \"2024\"`, so the export could not have been written any other way.\n\n## The two audits are complementary, and mine closes three of its caveats\n\nThe reviewer explicitly could not rule out three things, all of which my suite already covers:\n\n- *\"cannot rule out a different compiler/flag set exploiting the UB\"* → my 30-variant sweep (gcc/clang/cc × `-O0`…`-Ofast` × `-fwrapv`/`-fno-strict-overflow`/`-fstrict-overflow`/`-march=native`) all agree.\n- *\"a hypothetical logical-shift C implementation would differ\"* → same sweep covers gcc **and** clang; both use arithmetic shift.\n- *\"I compiled with rustc directly, not the cargo artifact\"* → every test here loads the actual cargo-produced `cdylib`, in both `debug` and `release`.\n\nIts one remaining caveat — that 2¹⁹² inputs can't be exhausted — is genuine and shared. I'd frame the mitigation honestly: I exhausted each parameter's **complete** 2³² domain individually plus the joint (multiplier × `step`) domain, and the 28/28 mutation score demonstrates the suite has real detection power. That is strong evidence, not a formal proof.\n\nNotably, the reviewer independently found **960,097** cases of the overwrite quirk via a different method, and Rust matched C on all of them — converging with my `row38` result from a completely different direction.\n\n## Final state\n\n- **73 tests** pass in both profiles, across both feature configurations\n- **43/43** `CONFIGS.md` rows, **20/20** `ERRORS.md` rows, symbol diff **empty (1/1)**\n- **~90.9 billion** differential comparisons from my suite; ~86 billion more from the independent audit\n- `c_src/` md5sums unchanged — sources never touched; only the required `c_src/build/` was added\n\nArtifacts in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md` (now 270 lines, including the cross-checked audit section), `scripts/check_all_features.sh`, and 8 test files.\n\nThe translation needed **no changes**. The only defects found in this entire exercise were three in my own artifacts — a false unreachability claim in `ERRORS.md`, an unreachable search region in one Phase B row, and a false-pass bug in the feature script — all fixed.","ttft_ms":10806,"ttft_stream_ms":2788,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":90350,"uuid":"0bd2bb24-80ed-45ac-a77e-b6c2e16bdb73","queued_turn_count":0}
